<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]operating_guidelines_savings

This table outlines the savings amounts offered for different types of cash services under operating guidelines, specifically for individuals, senior citizens/differently abled persons, and current account customers. The rows represent two distinct service types: 'Cash Pickup' and 'Cash Delivery', while the columns indicate varying savings tiers based on customer categories. For both services, individuals and senior citizens/differently abled persons receive a fixed savings amount of 20,000 per instance, whereas current account customers are entitled to 5 lacs per instance. This structure suggests a tiered benefit system where account type influences the level of financial incentive. The data is subject to change according to bank policy, as noted by the accompanying footnote. The table supports the context of door-step banking services and their operational flexibility, which can be executed by bank staff, vendors, or correspondents under agreed terms.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787125496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
